// Taking ownership of a heap box in a real-time region means FREEING it there, and `free` can block on the
// allocator lock exactly as `malloc` can. Nothing here is spelled like an allocation: `consume` has no
// `new`, no call, and its whole body is a getter — the defect is the parameter. Its control is
// tests/noheap_realtime_ok.kama, which BORROWS the object instead (`ref Node`) and is legal.
type resource Node { int32 v; public ctor make(int32 v) { this.v = v; } public fn int32 get() { return this.v; } }
@noheap fn int32 consume(Owned<Node> o) { return o.get(); }
fn int32 main() { Owned<Node> o = new Node.make(v: 5); return consume(o: give o); }
